WEBVTT

00:08.100 --> 00:11.030
Fall in love, boys and girls

00:11.570 --> 00:14.800
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

00:15.210 --> 00:18.270
The passion, the way it was born

00:18.740 --> 00:21.680
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

00:22.480 --> 00:25.500
How the hips shake, mucho dizzying

00:26.050 --> 00:29.180
Amigo, that's risky for a kid

00:29.620 --> 00:32.710
If I were to kiss, I'd get sucked in

00:33.190 --> 00:35.890
Tonight, I want to see something scary

00:36.930 --> 00:38.830
Don't be afraid

00:38.830 --> 00:40.500
Going from one push after another

00:40.500 --> 00:42.270
The surprising feeling is nice

00:42.270 --> 00:44.000
And you end up dancing till morning

00:44.000 --> 00:45.900
LOVE LOVE LOVE

00:45.900 --> 00:49.270
TROPICANA

00:51.310 --> 00:54.300
Catch me in the shade under the palm tree

00:55.040 --> 00:58.070
Make me wait, more than down to the limit

00:58.680 --> 01:01.580
I'm sorry, but you're already addicted

01:02.120 --> 01:05.250
From the jungle you can't escape! Haré+Guu!

01:05.890 --> 01:08.650
Fall in love, boys and girls

01:09.160 --> 01:12.360
Twinkle! Put a star in your eye

01:13.100 --> 01:16.190
The passion, the way it was born

01:16.570 --> 01:18.730
Makes sparks in the jungle! Haré+Guu!

01:23.780 --> 01:25.110
Sliced carp...

01:25.250 --> 01:26.610
Bream soup...

01:26.920 --> 01:28.380
Tuna carpaccio...

01:28.880 --> 01:31.320
Haré, look! They look tasty!

01:35.060 --> 01:38.860
Come to think of it,
I haven't eaten in quite a while...

01:39.800 --> 01:41.230
Tasty...

01:41.230 --> 01:42.960
F-I-S-H!

01:44.770 --> 01:46.500
You know, you're right.

01:46.970 --> 01:50.960
I want to eat fish!

01:51.040 --> 01:53.230
But, Ms. Yamada

01:56.250 --> 01:58.870
If she wants me to go fish,
she can say so outright.

01:59.410 --> 02:01.440
Geez, she went about it
in a very roundabout way.

02:02.420 --> 02:04.720
She thought she'd get the point across
without saying everything.

02:05.950 --> 02:08.180
She believes in her son's love for her.

02:09.990 --> 02:13.550
Well, if you think about it
that way it doesn't feel too bad, but...

02:14.500 --> 02:17.830
When you look at it objectively, you look
more like a slave than a son...

02:22.970 --> 02:24.200
Well, let's begin.

02:24.340 --> 02:25.240
Begin what?

02:25.340 --> 02:26.270
Fishing.

02:26.340 --> 02:27.370
What's fishing?

02:28.010 --> 02:30.980
You know, you put bait on like this...

02:31.950 --> 02:32.910
...and you toss it in.

02:34.350 --> 02:36.820
And when the fish bites, you pull it up.

02:37.150 --> 02:39.990
Well, just watch. I'm pretty good at this.

02:53.000 --> 02:53.930
Not yet?

02:54.000 --> 02:55.730
It's not something that happens instantly.

02:55.900 --> 02:57.740
You have to be more patient and wait.

03:17.490 --> 03:21.120
Come to think of it, it's been a while since I
was last alone with you, Guu.

03:22.230 --> 03:26.860
I breathe easier because I don't have to
worry about the people around us.

03:27.500 --> 03:31.130
Hey, wait! Why am I feeling
relaxed when I'm all alone with Guu?

03:32.570 --> 03:35.300
It's been a while
since we've been alone together.

03:35.410 --> 03:40.250
And for some reason, the conversation that
starts up sounds like an awkward couple
seeing each other for the first time in a while.

03:41.180 --> 03:42.380
How's it going?

03:42.480 --> 03:44.010
Is school fun?

03:44.120 --> 03:45.180
No, that's not it.

03:45.250 --> 03:49.190
This is more like a father trying to force a
conversation with his son.

03:49.520 --> 03:50.390
But, why?

03:51.790 --> 03:52.620
Oh!

03:52.730 --> 03:55.090
It's tugging, it's tugging!

04:02.300 --> 04:03.600
What is that?

04:04.070 --> 04:05.130
Eh? It's a fish.

04:05.840 --> 04:07.540
Oh, that's right.

04:07.640 --> 04:10.240
Guu, you've only seen fish
after they've been sliced apart.

04:10.410 --> 04:12.540
Fish all swim in the water.

04:16.650 --> 04:17.780
Oh...

04:22.390 --> 04:23.790
You need to catch these?

04:23.860 --> 04:24.350
Yup.

04:26.860 --> 04:28.830
Don't be too noisy. They'll swim away.

04:31.800 --> 04:32.660
One more time.

04:35.400 --> 04:37.670
I wonder if fish are unusual to her.

04:42.610 --> 04:45.270
Now, how many fish should I catch?

04:45.610 --> 04:47.610
Me, Mom, Guu...

04:47.720 --> 04:50.780
Guu always has leftovers,
but I'm sure Mom will eat it.

04:51.190 --> 04:53.590
If I catch a big one,
I'm sure Mom will be happy...

04:54.020 --> 04:56.680
I won't do anything fancy today.
I'll just salt-roast it.

05:01.560 --> 05:02.500
No way!

05:02.800 --> 05:04.820
She's kept her face
underwater for quite a while now...

05:04.900 --> 05:06.230
That means... she drowned?

05:06.600 --> 05:07.400
Hey! Guu!

05:08.040 --> 05:09.060
Guu!

05:09.240 --> 05:10.700
The fish swam away.

05:10.810 --> 05:13.500
Oh, I thought you had drowned...

05:18.250 --> 05:20.650
And now, after that big commotion...

05:21.980 --> 05:24.650
What!? What's up with that huge sigh!?

05:24.790 --> 05:26.250
In the first place, it was because
you did something that confused me!

05:26.320 --> 05:28.620
And now you're trying to shift the blame.

05:30.430 --> 05:32.390
I know that's what's going to happen.

05:32.790 --> 05:36.200
O-Oh well, everyone makes mistakes.

05:38.170 --> 05:39.900
You've grown up a little bit.

05:40.340 --> 05:42.960
Trying to get around
the situation by using ambiguous words.

05:43.770 --> 05:46.470
The bigger question is,
what to do about the fish.

05:47.140 --> 05:49.910
If we have only one,
we won't be able to make a meal of it.

05:50.480 --> 05:51.450
I've got no choice, then.

05:51.510 --> 05:52.980
I'll go catch some.

05:53.150 --> 05:54.380
You will, Guu?

05:54.450 --> 05:55.810
But, how?

05:56.220 --> 05:57.210
Hold this.

05:57.450 --> 05:58.480
S-Sure.

05:59.290 --> 06:00.220
What's this?

06:00.860 --> 06:02.760
Somehow, I know what this is about.

06:03.160 --> 06:05.250
That's right!
A cormorant! Cormorant fishing!

06:05.360 --> 06:08.020
It's when the cormorant swallows lots of fish,
then it's forced to throw them all back up!

06:08.100 --> 06:09.030
I've seen it on TV!

06:09.500 --> 06:10.930
Hey, Guu! Stop...

06:10.930 --> 06:11.930
Wait, she's already gone!

06:11.930 --> 06:14.990
Guu, stop that!
What happens if you drown!? Geez!

06:16.470 --> 06:18.170
Was the rope this long?

06:18.710 --> 06:19.570
Oof!

06:19.710 --> 06:20.570
Oh, Guu!

06:20.810 --> 06:22.000
Thank goodness!

06:22.080 --> 06:25.310
I was really worried
that you drowned or something!

06:25.380 --> 06:25.970
Really?

06:26.180 --> 06:27.710
I caught a lot of them.

06:27.850 --> 06:29.480
Eh? You caught?

06:29.920 --> 06:31.390
Can you rub my back?

06:31.490 --> 06:32.350
N-Noooooo!

06:35.990 --> 06:37.790
How far did you go?

06:37.960 --> 06:38.720
All sorts of places.

06:38.890 --> 06:41.450
But, where's the fish? The fish!

06:41.530 --> 06:43.760
The main objective,
the actual fish, isn't here at all!

06:48.000 --> 06:49.230
What the hell is this!?

06:49.370 --> 06:52.810
She was swimming all alone in the Genkai
Sea, so I couldn't help but swallow her.

06:52.870 --> 06:54.000
Restrain yourself and don't swallow her!

06:54.080 --> 06:55.700
In the first place,
would anyone swim with their clothes on!?

06:55.780 --> 06:57.180
No, she was swimming like this.

06:57.180 --> 06:58.700
That's called drowning!

06:59.710 --> 07:00.480
That means...

07:02.280 --> 07:03.150
Suicide?

07:05.020 --> 07:07.220
W-What should I do?
Should we let mom know?

07:07.220 --> 07:08.020
No, the police?

07:08.020 --> 07:09.590
Wait, but how can we explain this?

07:09.590 --> 07:11.630
I can't tell them that
she swallowed her up in the Genkai Sea!

07:11.630 --> 07:13.490
Or rather, where is this Genkai Sea?

07:13.860 --> 07:16.700
You can just ask someone
who understands and can take care of her.

07:16.970 --> 07:20.370
You make it sound so easy,
but do you know such convenient people?

07:20.470 --> 07:21.400
Seiichi and Tomoyo.

07:25.510 --> 07:26.910
And so...

07:28.410 --> 07:29.500
Let's go home.

07:29.610 --> 07:30.340
Oh, wait.

07:30.710 --> 07:31.410
What is it?

07:31.910 --> 07:34.680
Was it all right to do that?

07:34.780 --> 07:35.450
After all...

07:35.450 --> 07:36.050
You want her back out?

07:36.050 --> 07:36.880
No...

07:36.990 --> 07:39.480
I wouldn't know what to do
if you pull her back out...

07:39.550 --> 07:39.890
Then...

07:39.890 --> 07:40.550
Oh, but...

07:40.790 --> 07:41.520
Spit out?

07:41.520 --> 07:42.020
No, that's...

07:42.020 --> 07:42.360
Then...

07:42.360 --> 07:42.790
But, still...

07:42.790 --> 07:43.230
Spit out?

07:43.230 --> 07:43.790
But, still...

07:43.790 --> 07:44.060
Then...

07:44.060 --> 07:44.460
But...

07:44.460 --> 07:44.930
Out.

07:45.090 --> 07:45.330
No...

07:45.330 --> 07:45.590
But...

07:45.590 --> 07:45.860
Out.

07:45.860 --> 07:46.160
Eh?

07:46.390 --> 07:46.560
Oh...

07:46.560 --> 07:47.390
What to do?

07:47.900 --> 07:49.730
What should we do?

07:54.300 --> 07:55.000
Guu!

07:56.270 --> 07:57.240
Oh, Haré.

07:57.640 --> 07:58.610
Did a ball come this way?

07:59.370 --> 08:00.200
Gupta...

08:00.940 --> 08:02.310
Oh, here it is.

08:03.180 --> 08:04.440
We're playing dodgeball.

08:04.610 --> 08:05.550
You want to play with us?

08:08.880 --> 08:10.080
Hey, did you find the ball?

08:10.190 --> 08:11.580
Gupta, you're too strong.

08:11.690 --> 08:13.180
Hey, what's wrong?

08:13.460 --> 08:15.050
Did it hit, by any chance?

08:15.160 --> 08:16.950
Oh no... Is Guu all right?

08:17.060 --> 08:17.750
Get a grip!

08:17.830 --> 08:18.350
Guu!

08:20.460 --> 08:22.120
It's not my problem. Not my problem.

08:22.200 --> 08:23.890
When Guu gets angry, bad things follow.

08:23.970 --> 08:25.830
I'm sure she'll do in Gupta.

08:26.100 --> 08:28.070
I'm glad. You seem all right.

08:28.870 --> 08:30.800
Sorry about that. I didn't mean it.

08:30.870 --> 08:32.700
Well, forgive me. You're not mad, right?

08:33.840 --> 08:35.500
The quiet before the storm...

08:50.230 --> 08:52.060
C-Could this be!?

08:52.490 --> 08:53.290
The start of a battle?

08:54.130 --> 08:55.150
No, not good, not good!

08:55.260 --> 08:56.360
I have to do something.

08:56.500 --> 08:58.800
Hey, come on,
let's play Tarzan or something over there.

08:58.930 --> 09:00.660
Oh, let's do that. Let's go, let's go.

09:00.770 --> 09:01.700
Now, you too, Guu.

09:03.100 --> 09:06.780
I have to get them to play Tarzan, to get rid of
their stress.

09:06.780 --> 09:10.710
Wait, why do I have to stress out
in order to relieve other people's stress!?

09:10.780 --> 09:13.540
I don't have the time to say that, so for now...

09:14.250 --> 09:16.440
Who's going to be Tarzan?
Will it be Gupta after all?

09:16.550 --> 09:17.180
Of course.

09:17.250 --> 09:18.220
He's perfect for the role.

09:20.960 --> 09:21.790
Come on, Gupta.

09:21.860 --> 09:24.590
Hang onto that vine over there,
and make a really cool entrance.

09:24.990 --> 09:27.660
Now, fly to your heart's content,
and blow off that stress!

09:28.930 --> 09:29.990
I apologized.

09:30.070 --> 09:33.230
I apologized, so why do I have to
get a book thrown at me!?

09:33.300 --> 09:35.330
Oh, this irritates me!

09:38.670 --> 09:39.440
Gupta!

09:39.510 --> 09:40.910
Guu, are you all right?

09:41.310 --> 09:43.370
Please, stop that!

09:44.480 --> 09:47.040
Oh geez, what happens later will be really
scary...

09:47.580 --> 09:50.070
If it comes to this, I have to convince Guu.

09:53.260 --> 09:54.750
Guu, let's stop it here.

09:54.820 --> 09:56.790
Okay? Call it quits right now.

09:56.890 --> 10:00.160
I mean, Gupta apologized earlier...

10:00.160 --> 10:03.460
...and to be throwing something
of Ravenna's without her permission...

10:06.800 --> 10:08.270
Hey, what the hell is that!?

10:08.900 --> 10:10.630
I'm sure it's because
Gupta kept throwing things!

10:10.770 --> 10:12.360
I apologized!!

10:15.240 --> 10:15.900
What?

10:17.010 --> 10:18.210
No bullying.

10:19.510 --> 10:21.310
You're telling me not to bully him?

10:21.820 --> 10:24.680
Hey now, you're the one that threw Haré!

10:24.750 --> 10:25.380
FIG

10:26.620 --> 10:27.350
DURIAN

10:27.690 --> 10:28.390
Damn you!

10:28.390 --> 10:28.820
WHITE LONG-ARMED MONKEY

10:29.320 --> 10:29.790
ORANGUTAN

10:32.390 --> 10:33.090
N-Not good...

10:33.090 --> 10:35.930
I, the one called the "Abarenbo Shogun" of
the jungle...

10:35.930 --> 10:38.420
will suffer an absolute defeat at this rate.

10:39.200 --> 10:40.130
If that's the case...

10:40.400 --> 10:42.200
How about this!?

10:42.270 --> 10:43.000
RAFFLESIA

10:44.240 --> 10:45.170
MANEATER

10:47.580 --> 10:50.370
Hey now, does a creature like this
actually exist in this jungle?

10:53.620 --> 10:55.310
If it's come to this, I can't back down!

10:55.380 --> 10:56.870
I hope this hits!

10:58.150 --> 10:59.210
It's a hit and run!

11:04.990 --> 11:05.980
Oh, what should I do...

11:06.060 --> 11:08.150
At this rate,
Gupta will get eaten by the flower.

11:08.230 --> 11:09.630
But, can I stop this?

11:09.700 --> 11:11.690
Or rather, wouldn't I get sucked
into this as a victim also?

11:17.270 --> 11:18.100
There's no time to debate!

11:18.170 --> 11:19.870
It's going to be too late! Gupta!

11:20.340 --> 11:22.070
Guu! Gupta! Stop tha...

11:22.640 --> 11:25.240
Damn you! Take this!

11:28.880 --> 11:30.150
Haré!

11:30.790 --> 11:32.150
Wake up, Haré!

11:32.820 --> 11:34.080
Come on, wake up!

11:34.920 --> 11:35.650
Haré!

11:40.330 --> 11:41.320
Morning.

11:41.630 --> 11:42.560
Good morning!

11:44.030 --> 11:45.730
Wait, is that Seiichi and Tomoyo-san!?

11:45.800 --> 11:47.200
What are you doing outside?

11:47.270 --> 11:49.100
Where's Gupta? I have to stop Guu, too!

11:51.910 --> 11:53.670
Where is this?

11:53.840 --> 11:55.240
Well, it's not outside...

11:55.310 --> 11:56.400
It's rather, inside.

11:56.510 --> 11:57.770
I-Inside... you mean, of Guu?

11:57.980 --> 11:59.640
When was I swallowed up!?

11:59.880 --> 12:00.850
Just a few moments ago.

12:00.920 --> 12:02.180
We called for you.

12:02.280 --> 12:03.050
Don't call for me!

12:03.050 --> 12:04.850
Because we wanted your help.

12:04.950 --> 12:07.220
I can't help you guys at all!

12:09.860 --> 12:12.830
Haré, we thought that
you would definitely help us out.

12:12.930 --> 12:15.620
Yeah, this is a very serious problem.

12:16.330 --> 12:18.860
Considering how serious this might be,
you guys are talking very lightly.

12:19.330 --> 12:21.000
It's about that person.

12:21.100 --> 12:22.760
We're in a bit of a bind.

12:25.040 --> 12:26.130
Who is that person?

12:26.210 --> 12:27.940
Come on, don't forget already...

12:28.010 --> 12:29.370
It's the person
that you fished out, right Haré?

12:29.440 --> 12:31.180
Oh, that's right, that person back then...

12:31.180 --> 12:32.980
Wait a minute!
That wasn't me. That was Guu!

12:33.110 --> 12:35.050
Hey, can you do something about it?

12:35.550 --> 12:37.850
Y-You know, about that something...

12:37.850 --> 12:40.180
In the first place, why is she all tied up?

12:40.260 --> 12:41.880
Oh, that's because she's too violent.

12:41.960 --> 12:42.980
Violent!?

12:43.090 --> 12:45.650
She's really excited right now,
which causes us a lot of problems.

12:45.730 --> 12:47.350
We don't understand
what she's saying, either.

12:47.560 --> 12:50.790
That's why we want you
to talk to her to calm her down.

12:51.700 --> 12:52.630
No way!

12:52.700 --> 12:55.230
Me, a child, confronting a rabid person?

12:55.870 --> 12:57.360
It's perfect because you're a child.

12:58.310 --> 13:01.800
Yeah. We thought that she might open up her
heart a bit if she's talking to a kid.

13:02.340 --> 13:08.010
I'm sure that the pure, innocent soul of a
child will relieve her troubled feelings.

13:10.290 --> 13:11.120
You think so?

13:12.390 --> 13:12.940
Yeah!

13:13.490 --> 13:14.250
Yup, yup.

13:14.490 --> 13:17.950
This is something that only
you can do, Haré-kun. So, please?

13:21.530 --> 13:22.000
Please?

13:22.000 --> 13:22.860
We beg you.

13:22.860 --> 13:23.420
Please!

13:27.940 --> 13:29.730
Thanks. I knew we could
count on you, Haré-kun.

13:30.170 --> 13:31.160
We'll leave the rest to you.

13:31.410 --> 13:33.370
Good luck!

13:34.340 --> 13:36.610
Why can't I ever say no?

13:37.610 --> 13:39.840
Uh, now, act like a child, like a child...

13:40.580 --> 13:42.880
U-Um, hello.

13:43.590 --> 13:46.050
Nice to meet you.

13:46.120 --> 13:48.590
I'm not anyone suspicious.

13:48.660 --> 13:52.750
If you don't mind,
could we talk for a little while?

13:52.860 --> 13:54.350
He doesn't sound much like a child.

13:54.500 --> 13:55.390
You're right.

13:57.000 --> 13:58.360
Oh, it worked?

14:00.070 --> 14:01.590
Are you someone from this place, too?

14:03.940 --> 14:05.270
I guess you could say that.

14:06.540 --> 14:09.070
I'm sorry I'm in this state.

14:09.740 --> 14:12.410
I was out of control until a few minutes ago.

14:13.180 --> 14:15.950
I really troubled those two people...

14:16.020 --> 14:18.280
N-no, but why did you?

14:20.150 --> 14:23.560
I was dumped by the division chief...

14:24.090 --> 14:28.260
...and got sick of everything
in this world, and tried to die.

14:28.430 --> 14:30.690
Oh, that's why you were in the ocean.

14:32.970 --> 14:35.230
He was married, and had children...

14:35.600 --> 14:37.940
I didn't think that he would choose me at all.

14:38.470 --> 14:39.670
But...

14:40.340 --> 14:42.740
I was really serious about him.

14:43.080 --> 14:44.840
That's a typical plot for an affair.

14:45.350 --> 14:47.510
But, you shouldn't plunge into the ocean.

14:48.080 --> 14:50.020
You need to cherish your life.

14:51.820 --> 14:52.680
Yes...

14:52.790 --> 14:55.950
Oh, she's a pretty normal woman
if you talk to her normally.

14:56.660 --> 14:59.020
Oh, I'm calm now, so can you untie this?

14:59.160 --> 15:00.130
Oh, sure.

15:01.700 --> 15:04.060
He's untying her hands,
but I wonder if that's okay...

15:04.570 --> 15:07.000
I'm sure he succeeded in convincing her.

15:07.500 --> 15:08.870
Are you all right?

15:09.270 --> 15:10.790
There, it's all undone.

15:11.470 --> 15:14.240
What was that about
a typical plot for an affair!?

15:14.310 --> 15:16.710
Damn brat speaking like he knows it all!

15:16.710 --> 15:17.800
Is she a different person!?

15:18.280 --> 15:19.680
The chief, too!

15:19.750 --> 15:22.380
Being able to date someone this beautiful
should be enough to send him to heaven!

15:22.480 --> 15:24.820
Oh! To break up with me!

15:26.390 --> 15:29.220
Miss, you really have so much energy for
someone who wanted to die...

15:29.360 --> 15:30.420
Of course I do!

15:30.690 --> 15:37.720
I was so ready to turn into a ghost
and curse that perverted old geezer
to the last of his descendants!

15:38.300 --> 15:39.230
CURSE

15:39.230 --> 15:40.470
T-That's Different

15:40.470 --> 15:43.370
The reason that she wants to die
is different from everyone else's

15:43.710 --> 15:44.540
But...

15:45.170 --> 15:48.110
I was pathetic, and couldn't die,
and kept living on...

15:48.540 --> 15:53.210
But I can't continue to live on
pathetically and face my parents.

15:53.210 --> 15:54.910
And, I can't stay
at that company anymore, either.

15:55.820 --> 15:59.480
But, to me, it was true love!

15:59.620 --> 16:00.550
I waited!

16:00.620 --> 16:02.920
I kept waiting for his true love!

16:02.920 --> 16:07.590
I swore to my heart that I will withstand all
the harsh waves of the Genkai Sea!

16:07.800 --> 16:09.660
But, I got dumped.

16:10.870 --> 16:13.890
Yes, I was the dumb one!

16:14.000 --> 16:18.410
Such a dumb person like me has no right to
keep living in this world...

16:18.640 --> 16:22.870
Oh, the tragic heroine -
Yamada Hiroko, 22 years old!

16:23.010 --> 16:28.010
Someone, please come down
to give me a romantic death!

16:28.420 --> 16:29.580
N-No good...

16:29.580 --> 16:31.920
I can't hold a decent conversation with her...

16:32.220 --> 16:33.950
Seiichi-san, can I have a minute?

16:35.490 --> 16:39.220
Well, I really can't do anything,
other than cheer you on.

16:39.330 --> 16:40.420
Fight!

16:40.530 --> 16:42.260
Aren't you running away, a bit there?

16:42.960 --> 16:47.200
When you untie her hands, she totally gets
the people around her involved...

16:47.200 --> 16:51.040
...and then plunges into her own little world
where she cries and screams.

16:51.140 --> 16:52.570
So be careful!

16:52.670 --> 16:54.110
Say that beforehand!

16:58.210 --> 17:00.050
For now, I need to make a run for it myself.

17:00.050 --> 17:00.910
Wait!

17:01.480 --> 17:03.680
Please, I beg you...

17:03.750 --> 17:07.210
Before you go away somewhere, kill me.

17:09.160 --> 17:12.250
It's too tough to keep on living.

17:13.900 --> 17:14.830
Miss...

17:16.030 --> 17:16.890
Please...

17:21.070 --> 17:23.900
You say that, but when you die, you're going
to curse that division chief, right?

17:24.070 --> 17:25.040
Of course I will.

17:26.110 --> 17:30.370
But, isn't it a little lonely
to die cursing someone?

17:30.610 --> 17:31.580
No.

17:31.580 --> 17:35.320
I think every person in this world
other than myself should become
as unhappy as I've been.

17:35.320 --> 17:36.940
You really are evil
from the bottom of your heart...

17:38.190 --> 17:40.590
But, that's such a waste.

17:41.990 --> 17:45.490
Y-You know, although I'm just a kid...

17:45.490 --> 17:51.020
I think you're really pretty, miss,
so I think it's a waste for you to die.

17:52.570 --> 17:53.500
You think so?

17:53.670 --> 17:54.500
Yeah.

17:54.570 --> 17:57.900
Besides, you're still really young at 22.

17:58.710 --> 18:01.470
I'm sure there are plenty of better things
waiting for you in the future.

18:02.710 --> 18:04.140
In the future...

18:04.880 --> 18:06.870
Yeah, in the future.

18:07.580 --> 18:10.110
We still have tomorrow ahead of us.

18:27.100 --> 18:29.130
You can't keep living
unless you think that way.

18:29.270 --> 18:31.500
You make it sound
so practical when you say that.

18:32.110 --> 18:33.630
Of course it does.

18:33.780 --> 18:36.240
When Mom says
she wants to eat fish, I go fishing.

18:36.680 --> 18:38.910
I get worried about
whether or not Guu is drowning.

18:39.110 --> 18:42.110
When I tried to save Gupta,
without thinking about my own safety...

18:42.550 --> 18:43.950
I ended up in this situation.

18:45.520 --> 18:47.390
Geez! Listen to me, miss!

18:47.390 --> 18:47.910
Y-Yes?

18:48.260 --> 18:50.660
You know, I just turned 11 the other day...

18:50.660 --> 18:52.860
...yet I have to worry about what everyone
around me is thinking each and every day!

18:52.860 --> 18:54.960
The guy who is supposedly my dad is the
worst guy, and my mom is a sloth!

18:54.960 --> 18:58.730
All my friends and acquaintances are
strange, never giving me peace of mind!

18:58.800 --> 19:00.640
Among them,
there's one stickler of a character...

19:00.640 --> 19:03.910
...and she always, always, always, always,
always, always does things that I don't like!

19:03.910 --> 19:06.430
Or rather, she eats me up
like this once in a while!

19:06.570 --> 19:09.140
Are there normally people out there that
would eat their friends!?

19:09.140 --> 19:10.970
Oh, I'm so sick of it!!

19:11.410 --> 19:13.010
You face tough times, too.

19:13.010 --> 19:14.380
Tough, tough, tough!!

19:15.120 --> 19:18.210
Even small kids like him have their worries.

19:18.450 --> 19:19.920
It wasn't just me.

19:21.020 --> 19:23.490
But, you know, even in such a life...

19:23.490 --> 19:25.690
I find small happinesses,
and do my best to live on.

19:25.860 --> 19:28.620
So, I want you to do
your best as well, miss. Okay?

19:28.960 --> 19:31.560
Are those really tears of happiness?

19:32.270 --> 19:34.890
It's all about believing
in the happiness tomorrow brings.

19:35.770 --> 19:37.530
That's right.

19:37.610 --> 19:39.400
I guess I should try a little harder.

19:39.470 --> 19:43.710
When I think about it,
it might have been a good thing
that I broke up with such a worthless guy.

19:43.910 --> 19:46.550
That's right!
I'm sure you'll meet someone new!

19:46.550 --> 19:50.150
That's right! The men of this world wouldn't
ignore such a beautiful woman!

19:50.150 --> 19:51.850
All right! I'm gonna go for it!
There still is tomorrow!

19:51.850 --> 19:53.450
All right! I'm gonna go for it!
There still is tomorrow!
The two of them...

19:53.450 --> 19:56.160
All right! I'm gonna go for it!
Come on, we should try our best!
...are forgetting one key issue.

19:56.160 --> 19:57.280
Come on, we should try our best!

19:57.630 --> 20:00.220
I don't know why, but I feel really refreshed!

20:00.290 --> 20:01.430
Me, too.

20:01.430 --> 20:04.020
I think it's because
we were able to release all our worries.

20:04.130 --> 20:06.570
All right, let's make
a dash towards tomorrow!

20:08.740 --> 20:09.700
Hurray!

20:09.700 --> 20:12.300
Oh, wait, I won't lose!

20:15.280 --> 20:16.540
Hurray!

20:36.660 --> 20:39.000
I'm back...

20:40.130 --> 20:42.970
This time, victory is mine for sure! Take this!

20:47.980 --> 20:48.740
How's this!?

20:55.720 --> 20:56.980
This is weird.

21:03.320 --> 21:05.520
Eh? Is this a happy ending? Is this okay?

21:06.560 --> 21:07.430
NEXT EPISODE

21:07.430 --> 21:10.000
That's right, stay up all night playing games,
reading manga, eating potato chips, and drinking cola!

21:12.130 --> 21:12.660
Eh? Mom is missing?

21:12.660 --> 21:15.800
What do you mean? Why would Mom end up
missing? She got lost during the hunt!?

21:15.800 --> 21:17.470
She was assaulted by a creature that nobody
has ever seen before?

21:17.470 --> 21:18.540
What kind of a creature was it?

21:18.540 --> 21:22.070
Eh? Some creature that's black, big, hard,
shiny, smelly, and makes a strange noise?

21:18.970 --> 21:21.000
Actually, where is this?

21:21.440 --> 21:22.070
Where are the people?

21:22.070 --> 21:22.940
What's that?

21:22.140 --> 21:23.610
It's just us two.

21:23.580 --> 21:25.610
Next episode of Haré+Guu:

21:25.610 --> 21:29.250
Smelly, Noise-Making Creature

21:29.250 --> 21:31.220
Smelly, Noise-Making Creature

21:31.220 --> 21:31.840
Smelly, Noise-Making Creature
